          production:"CANE MILLING: Harvested cane is crushed between rollers; juice extracted with water. Juice clarified with lime (Ca(OH)₂) → clarified juice evaporated to thick syrup in multiple-effect evaporators → seeded with sugar crystals in vacuum pans → massecuite (crystal+mother liquor) centrifuged → raw sugar (96–98% sucrose) + molasses. RAW SUGAR REFINING (to white): Raw sugar dissolved in water (affination, then melt clarification with lime and CO₂/phosphoric acid). Liquor decolorized with activated carbon or ion exchange. Recrystallized in vacuum pans → refined white sugar (99.7–99.9% sucrose). BEET SUGAR: Beets sliced into cossettes, juice extracted by countercurrent diffusion, immediately purified and crystallized — no raw sugar intermediate; goes straight to white sugar.",
