          summary:"The world's most produced organic chemical (~200M t/year). Produced by steam cracking. Foundation of the entire petrochemical chain — polyethylene, PVC, polyester, and more.",
          production:"STEAM CRACKING: Ethane, propane, or naphtha is mixed with steam and heated to 800–850°C in pyrolysis furnaces for 0.1–0.5 seconds (very short residence time to avoid coking). Hydrocarbon bonds break (cracking) to produce ethylene, propylene, butadiene, and other olefins. The cracked gas is quenched, compressed, and separated by a series of distillation columns in a complex Cold Box fractionation train (temperatures down to -160°C). FURNACE DECOKING: Coke deposits burn periodically with steam/air.",
